infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why the alias works in ORDER BY but not WHERE
  desc A SELECT alias is born in step 5 — clauses before it can't name it, clauses at or after it can
  compares
    - label Runs before SELECT — alias not yet created
      children
        - label WHERE (step 2)
          desc Filters raw columns; naming the alias raises ERROR: column does not exist
        - label GROUP BY (step 3)
          desc Before projection by the SQL standard; alias works only as a Postgres extension
        - label HAVING (step 4)
          desc Filters groups before SELECT; standard SQL forbids the alias here
    - label Runs at or after SELECT — alias is available
      children
        - label SELECT (step 5)
          desc Projection evaluates price * qty AS revenue — the alias is created here
        - label ORDER BY (step 7)
          desc Sorts the projected output, so ORDER BY revenue resolves cleanly
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
